To add: if there is ambiguity in CLL as to the shape of acceptable 
fu'ivla etc., the BPFK can step in and disambiguate.. If the CLL 
clearly states "shape X is experimental only", I don't think the BPFK 
should make such experimental shapes  official, since noone yet but 
the petitioner has used those experimental shapes extensively (let's 
be blunt here): the time for experimentality is not yet passed.

But like I say, we'll consider anything --- and reject most things, 
if I have anything to do with it. This is a fundamentalist endeavour. 
And we'll see what the voting body ends up looking like.
